OL,3,GNEWSAMy son was jailed indefinitely for
OL,4,Astealing a mobile - we've waited 21
OL,5,Ayears to see him released
OL,6,
OL,7,F"It's like your son being killed - he's
OL,8,Fhere but he's not."
OL,10,FLeroy Douglas was just 24 when he was
OL,11,Fjailed in 2005 for stealing a mobile
OL,12,Fphone and handed a minimum prison term
OL,13,Fof two-and-a-half years.
OL,15,FMore than 20 years later, he is still
OL,16,Flocked up.
